-Let us begin by first setting up the notation. Let $\mathcal{H}$ be a finite-dimensional Hilbert space. We denote the set of density matrices on $\mathcal{H}$ as $\psd{\mathcal{H}}$. The set of density matrices which are \emph{strictly positive} is denoted as $\pd{\mathcal{H}}$. For simplicity, throughout the paper, we focus on the cases where the density matrices are strictly positive definite. We expect a generalization of our results for positive semi-definite density matrices would require a projection onto an appropriate subspace, which we leave for future work.
